  "answer": "To study the presence of starch in leaves, the following process is followed in the laboratory: first, a leaf is boiled in water to kill the cells and then boiled in methylated spirit to remove chlorophyll. After that, the leaf is spread on a petridish and a few drops of iodine solution are added. If starch is present, the leaf turns bluish-black. This process helps in identifying the presence of starch in the leaf.",
